---
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { page } from '../config/pages';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const hosted = site.cloudLaunched
  ? 'The hosted service is open for sign-ups and is paid for by subscriptions, with accounts, billing, two-factor sign-in, automatic backups and email check-ins.'
  : 'The hosted service is about to open and will be paid for by subscriptions. Its accounts, billing, two-factor sign-in, automatic backups and email are planned, not running.';
---

<PageLayout
  {...page('/about/')}
  heading="A planner you can see inside"
  eyebrow="About"
  lede="Glideworth is an independent, open-source financial and retirement planner. It exists for people who want to understand their plan, not just receive a number, and who want to keep control of their financial data."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' }]}
>
  <div class="container-narrow body">
    <Prose>
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Planning for retirement comes down to one question: will my money last, and what can I change? Most tools answer
        the first half with a number and leave you to trust it. Glideworth tries to answer both halves and show the
        working. Every year of a projection has a ledger, every tax estimate lists what it leaves out, and every result
        can be traced to what produced it.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is also built so that software can help. A complete REST API and an MCP server let scripts and AI assistants
        read your plan, run simulations and propose changes that you approve, without being able to overwrite anything.
      </p>

      <h2>What we believe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Show the working.</strong> The <a href="/features/projections-and-ledger/">ledger</a> and the <a href="/features/explanations-and-audit/">explanations</a> are the product, not an extra.</li>
        <li><strong>Your data, your choice of computer.</strong> The full planner is open source and runs on your own machine if you prefer. See <a href="/self-hosting/">self-hosting</a> and <a href="/security/">security</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Estimates, honestly labelled.</strong> Glideworth models your assumptions. Tax figures are estimates for stated tax years, and each country lists <a href="/blog/what-a-tax-estimate-leaves-out/">what it leaves out</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Nothing held back.</strong> The self-hosted build has every feature. The hosted service sells convenience. See <a href="/open-source/">open source</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <p>
        Glideworth is an independent project, not part of a bigger company, and it is maintained by very few people. We
        have not put a team page here because there is no more to say than that, and we would rather say nothing than
        invent something. Glideworth is the product and trading name of {site.entity.name}, {site.entity.description}. The
        contributor and licensing rules are public, and anyone can read the code in the <a href={site.repoUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">source repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What it is not</h2>
      <p>
        Glideworth is planning software. It is not a financial adviser, a tax return or a regulated service, and it does
        not tell you what to buy. It does not connect to your bank, sell your data or run advertising. Talk to a
        qualified adviser before you act on a projection.
      </p>

      <h2>Where things stand</h2>
      <p>
        The planner works today and you can self-host it. {hosted}
        The <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a> says what comes next, with no dates, and the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>
        records what has actually changed. To reach us, see <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
  <CTABand />
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .body {
    padding-bottom: var(--section-y);
  }
</style>
